message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Symbiotic World: selection on how organisms learn, in a persistent 3D ecosystem"
abstract: >-
  A persistent 3D ecosystem in Unreal Engine 5.7 in which every organism learns online across its
  own lifetime with a tabular contextual bandit, and offspring inherit how it learns — step size,
  exploration rate, sociality and an environmental-effect strength — with mutation, so selection
  acts on the learning itself. A neutral-drift control mode runs the identical world with
  reproduction decoupled from fitness. Above the simulation sits the Symbiotic Lab, a team of
  language-model scientist agents that registers hypotheses, preregisters predictions, runs
  controlled experiments against the simulation's own parameters and scores itself.
